{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>The impure.</b> For the Tanna who does not derive the impurity of their skins from ״הַטְּמֵאִים״ — why is it needed? Our Sages of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim, Shemini, chapter 7) that it comes to include the egg of a creeping creature that has begun to develop. They also derived (Torat Kohanim there; Me'ilah 17a) that blood combines with blood, blood with flesh, whether of one species or of two species, for impurity." "And one must understand the word <b>אֵלֶּה</b> — what does it come to exclude according to its way? And it appears to explain it according to what the Rambam wrote in chapter 4 of Hilkhot Avot ha-Tum'ah: the blood of a creeping creature is like its flesh and combines to the size of a lentil as long as it is attached to its flesh. Therefore it says ״אֵלֶּה״ to exclude — if the blood separated from the creeping creature it does not combine with the flesh."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:23.828346669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}